toastman@armory.com (Powdered Toast Man) writes:

>I find it quite helpful having all those potions of healing and whatnot.
>I usually don't find stethoscopes, but there were several for sale in the 
>mine town., which quickly replaced the wand of probing I had earlier 
>(though I used it twice since then before getting killed)

Wand of probing is nowhere near as useful as the stethoscope.  For one
thing, if I'm not mistaken, the Wand actually takes a turn to apply,
which severely limits its utility in combat.  The stethoscope can be
used freely without time passing.  Plus, the Wand has a very limited number
of charges.  I wind up using my stethoscope approximately one zillion times
per game, which I believe exceeds the maximum number of charges on a wand.

>I was wondering exactly how accurate the stethoscope was?  Or what if it 
>was cursed?  Because for some reason, it kept reporting an INCREASED 
>amount of maximum hit points every time I used it on a brown mold I was 
>trying to kill.  Never know when cold resistance will come in handy, I 
>always say, but this thing got stronger and stronger!  weeird.

The stethoscope is absolutely accurate.  If it's cursed, you sometimes get
the message "You hear your heart beat" instead.  (Incedentally, ever
tried applying a stethoscope to yourself?  It's a cheap way to find out
how well-aligned you are.)  As for the brown mold...well, you have now
learned something about how brown molds work.  Every time they hit you,
they get a little stronger.

